{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition","id":528989,"title":"What's new in 2nd edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-26T11:10:00-07:00","id":528989,"title":"What's new in 2nd edition?","content":"I'm pondering to buy The Forsaken 2nd Edition, but before to spend money I would like to be enlighted about the differences between the 1st and 2nd edition. Thank you very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:50:39-07:00","id":529077,"title":"","content":"Um. A lot.<br /> <br /> Obviously the change over to the 2e nWOD ruleset (which is fully in the WtF 2e core book, you don't need to buy anything else), which you can get a free preview of with the free download of the God-Machine Chronicles Rules Update (GMCRU) pdf. Conditions and Tilts in particular were integrated strongly into Forsaken 2e.<br /> <br /> The biggest thematic change is refocusing on werewolves as hunters. It frames a lot of the game.<br /> <br /> Auspices now have a &quot;Hunter's Aspect&quot; which lets them inflict Conditions on targets they're hunting appropriate to their Auspice (so the Cahalith one terrifies prey into being the victim of the hunt, while the Irraka one makes them oblivious to the hunt about to strike them). The Auspice powers are generally a bit more potent.<br /> <br /> Harmony has completely reworked to emphasize balance. The &quot;ideal&quot; is now 5 instead of 10, with 10 and1 being extremes that come with drawbacks (though can be worth heading towards sometimes. You don't spend XP on Harmony, if you want to move in a direction you act more appropriately towards it. It's also not the base-line for dice-pools any more.<br /> <br /> Renown has more oomph so it feels worth having on it's own, rather than just a gate on your Gifts. A big factor is the ability to flair your Renown (another Condition generator) that encourages your pack to challenge you're skills, but drives you to perform even better.<br /> <br /> Packs themselves are more broad now, with Wolf-blooded and humans being part of packs by default (even in human members aren't always in the know of what they're involved with).<br /> <br /> Wolf-Blooded are much more variable, each coming in with a Tell, that defines a drawback of their wolf-blood, but also provides them a useful power. Wolf-blooded can also be generated by exposing normal humans to Lunacy.<br /> <br /> Death rage is now a two stage process, with a &quot;soft&quot; starting point and the &quot;hard&quot; full on death rage slaughter-fest. Packs need to be careful since death rage can be emotionally infectious within the pack setting off a chain reaction. Triggers and how long the soft phase lasts before you completely freak out are based on Harmony.<br /> <br /> Unihar are out. Werewolves can have kids without any spiritual consequences.<br /> <br /> Gifts and Rites have been reworked considerably. Auspice-specific (Moon) Gifts mostly work like they used to (1-5 powers) but you get them automatically when you get more Renown. Shadow Gifts (most of the standard Gifts) are not 1-5 powers, but five powers clustered around a theme; one for each Renown called a Facet. When you buy a Gift, you unlock access to its five Facets if you have the Renown for them. Wolf Gifts are unlocked automatically so you can get the Facets more easily/cheaper than Shadow Gifts. Facets generally scale with their associated Renown (including Moon Gift Facets).<br /> <br /> Rites aren't treated like Gifts and are simply bought with XP, and everyone starts with some. Rites are also not restricted solely to Uratha. Some are pack rites that are available to the right Wolf-blooded (but benefit anyone associate that's part of the pack).<br /> <br /> The Sacred Hunt rite is also a very key aspect (though not essential) to the game. Each Tribe has a favored prey and gets special perks for calling the Sacred Hunt on that prey.<br /> <br /> All the five forms have more distinct purposes and benefits.<br /> <br /> And more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T12:36:00-07:00","id":529129,"title":"","content":"Werewolves can now have creatures and people other than other werewolves in their packs - making them less Forsaken than in first edition.They also can go to their own kind for comfort, also making them less Forsaken than in first edition. <br /> <br /> The sense of horror and urgency from the previous edition is gone, largely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T12:43:37-07:00","id":529134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529129#post529129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sense of horror and urgency from the previous edition is gone, largely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's really fair to say, specially given how much more emphasis is placed on the inhuman, predatorial outlook of the Uratha, and the truly vicious and terrifying enemies they face*. Far as I'm concerned, a great part of the horror in the 2e book comes from how the writing has a growing dissonance from human values as you progress that truly casts even the Forsaken themselves, with their interests aligned for the wellbeing of both the physical world and the Shadow, as monsters.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Though the Prey chapter really could use some expansion, because there's so much about each of the Forsaken's enemies (other than the Idigam) that deserves significant wordcount to explore and elaborate on. Nonetheless, they are well introduced, and we'll likely see a future book (or books) with more detail.</span></span><br /> <br /> Some of the <i>isolation</i> seems gone or lightened, yes. But not entirely. The Forsaken are still fighting constantly on every front, even against those who would be their kin. Their only sure allies, their only sure support, is their pack. They often hunt enemies bigger and nastier than themselves, and the only way they can even those odds is with their pack. They are wolves as much as they are spirits, after all, and wolves are pack animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-26-2015, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:04:30-07:00","id":529171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529129#post529129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves can now have creatures and people other than other werewolves in their packs - making them less Forsaken than in first edition.They also can go to their own kind for comfort, also making them less Forsaken than in first edition. <br /> <br /> The sense of horror and urgency from the previous edition is gone, largely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one person's opinion, and it is definitely not shared by most of the people on these forums (for whatever that's worth). The personal horror just comes from things other than not being able to Boink your own kind (which I never found especially horrifying, personally). At any rate, if you dislike those changes, you can easily just say non-werewolves can't join packs and Unihar are still a thing. Sticking to 1e rules because you don't like a few minor fluff changes is a serious case of throwing the baby out with the bath water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:09:26-07:00","id":529176,"title":"","content":"I know I can stick to 1st edition; I do. I was answering the first poster's question. <br /> <br /> The fluff changes aren't minor to me. They make the game unappealing to me. You are free to disagree of course; I'm glad you like the 2nd edition. I hope you get to have lots of fun with the game. I'll stick with the first edition, because it's a whole lot closer to my ideal Werewolf game than 2nd edition, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:15:04-07:00","id":529178,"title":"","content":"Sense of horror gone?<br /> <br /> Idigam are a thing, y'know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:20:45-07:00","id":529182,"title":"","content":"Yeah? They've been a thing in first edition too. <br /> <br /> It's not gone. It's, in this poster's opinion, gone, largely, because the Forsaken in 2nd edition have it easier than the Forsaken in 1st edition. <br /> <br /> It's like this - the first edition of the game is a horror game. It's established right in the corebook that I have in front of me right now - the Forsaken are exactly that, Forsaken. There's a strong sense of desperation in the setting - the Forsaken have been outnumbered by the Pure ever since the Brethren War. The idigam are back. There's also plenty of elaboration of the downsides of being a werewolf - the rage, the many things werewolves are afraid of, especially about themselves. <br /> <br /> The 2nd edition book doesn't spend too much time talking about that. The protagonists of the second edition don't have it that hard. There are gaps in the storytelling section of the book, a section that, in my opinion, should really address the downsides of the Forsaken condition, and, again in my opinion, fails to do so. <br /> <br /> I far too often catch myself thinking that 2nd edition presents its protagonists in a glorifying, celebratory light that didn't exist in the first edition. The book emphasizes the upsides of the werewolf condition in ways that make me uncomfortable at times. It shouldn't be great to be a werewolf. It shouldn't be great to experience the rage and the hunger for flesh and the desire to hunt. The first edition of the game doesn't suffer from this particular problem. Blood and Smoke, a game that I like much better than the first edition of Vampire, really absolutely doesn't suffer from this particular problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:22:49-07:00","id":529188,"title":"","content":"Personally, Idigam are not all that horrifying to me. They are definitely not what I want in a game, as they are not needed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:26:20-07:00","id":529191,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the Idigam - I think they're interesting. I do think, however, that the setting has antagonists that are even more interesting - Spiders that enter the human body via orifices, eat your brain and move your body around the way people drive cars. Spiritual manifestations of your own deepest fears and passions. Cunning, sly spirit beings hiding in the souls of your friends and loved ones, corrupting their minds and bodies from the inside. Raging fanatics in werewolf skin who want you dead because they can't overcome their own moral failings. That sort of thing. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:28:39-07:00","id":529194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529182#post529182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah? They've been a thing in first edition too.<br /> <br /> It's not gone. It's, in this poster's opinion, gone, largely, because the Forsaken in 2nd edition have it easier than the Forsaken in 1st edition.<br /> <br /> It's like this - the first edition of the game is a horror game. It's established right in the corebook that I have in front of me right now - the Forsaken are exactly that, Forsaken. There's a strong sense of desperation in the setting - the Forsaken have been outnumbered by the Pure ever since the Brethren War. The idigam are back. There's also plenty of elaboration of the downsides of being a werewolf - the rage, the many things werewolves are afraid of, especially about themselves.<br /> <br /> The 2nd edition book doesn't spend too much time talking about that. The protagonists of the second edition don't have it that hard. There are gaps in the storytelling section of the book, a section that, in my opinion, should really address the downsides of the Forsaken condition, and, again in my opinion, fails to do so.<br /> <br /> I far too often catch myself thinking that 2nd edition presents its protagonists in a glorifying, celebratory light that didn't exist in the first edition. The book emphasizes the upsides of the werewolf condition in ways that make me uncomfortable at times. It shouldn't be great to be a werewolf. It shouldn't be great to experience the rage and the hunger for flesh and the desire to hunt. The first edition of the game doesn't suffer from this particular problem. Blood and Smoke, a game that I like much better than the first edition of Vampire, really absolutely doesn't suffer from this particular problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the horror is more refined this time around, and not as much of a slog: You're right, 2E Forsaken have it slightly easier in that they actually have outlets that they can express themselves through. But those necessarily drive them away from humanity. Life can't be 100% awful all the time, even for a werewolf. The problem is, those things in your life that you can actually enjoy serve as a reminder that you're not human.<br /> <br /> I prefer Promethean for my &quot;Stymied at every attempt to try and fit in&quot; horror. Werewolf should be about balancing humanity with spirit, which 2E does much better than 1E. The horror is that becoming too much of either turns you into an indiscriminate engine of murder. Making the pack a place that you can undisputably call a Home means that you have stakes and urgency.<br /> <br /> I know you disagree, and I'm not trying to persuade you otherwise: I just feel like 2E does horror and urgency <i>better</i>, and that's why I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:34:17-07:00","id":529199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529194#post529194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the horror is more refined this time around, and not as much of a slog: You're right, 2E Forsaken have it slightly easier in that they actually have outlets that they can express themselves through. But those necessarily drive them away from humanity. Life can't be 100% awful all the time, even for a werewolf. The problem is, those things in your life that you can actually enjoy serve as a reminder that you're not human.<br /> <br /> I prefer Promethean for my &quot;Stymied at every attempt to try and fit in&quot; horror. Werewolf should be about balancing humanity with spirit, which 2E does much better than 1E. The horror is that becoming too much of either turns you into an indiscriminate engine of murder. Making the pack a place that you can undisputably call a Home means that you have stakes and urgency.<br /> <br /> I know you disagree, and I'm not trying to persuade you otherwise: I just feel like 2E does horror and urgency <i>better</i>, and that's why I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respect that. I prefer things if packs cannot ever include anything other than werewolves and a pack totem - the Forsaken are less Forsaken, in my opinion, if there are people in their pack - there is fewer reason for them to interact with ordinary people - less of a sense of isolation; which really isn't good for the setting. <br /> <br /> It's a matter of taste, quite naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:35:49-07:00","id":529201,"title":"","content":"True. &quot;oh, no I could lose control and hurt someone I care about&quot; loses a lot of bite when <i>nobody fits that description. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:46:03-07:00","id":529224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529182#post529182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The book emphasizes the upsides of the werewolf condition in ways that make me uncomfortable at times. It shouldn't be great to be a werewolf. It shouldn't be great to experience the rage and the hunger for flesh and the desire to hunt.</b> The first edition of the game doesn't suffer from this particular problem. Blood and Smoke, a game that I like much better than the first edition of Vampire, really absolutely doesn't suffer from this particular problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually a great part of the subtle horror in the writing for me. I like how the book goes about that. It's the growing dissonance from human values thing I mentioned before.<br /> <br /> You're right that it's not done in Vampire 2e (or at least not nearly as much). The grim downsides of the vampiric condition are layed down much more explicitely there in comparison to being a werewolf in 2e, and what is said contributes a lot to its atmosphere of personal horror. But IMHO, the way Werewolf handles it <i>works</i>. And the reason it works is because Werewolves are just that sort of instinct-driven being. They're not like Vampires, who are in their monstrous nature more cold and detached despite the inner presence of their Beast. Werewolves are inherently predators that deep down are supposed to exult in the things you mentioned.<br /> <br /> You're in your right to disagree, to just not like that tone, or to think it doesn't fit your image of Werewolf The Forsaken. But I don't think it's correct to say that the horror is lacking in the writing, even in comparison to the 1st edition. It's at the relevant points, simply presented in a different manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:47:27-07:00","id":529240,"title":"","content":"I think I've been respectful in my statement of preference concerning the two editions of the same game; I wish others would be so likewise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:50:28-07:00","id":529243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529201#post529201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. &quot;oh, no I could lose control and hurt someone I care about&quot; loses a lot of bite when <i>nobody fits that description. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I will continue this line of discussion after you've reread the setting chapter of the first edition book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:52:08-07:00","id":529246,"title":"","content":"If that came off as disrespectful I assure you that wasn't the intention. I apologize.<br /> <br /> Was just trying to make clear that the division between personal preference and recognizing the aim and quality of the writing within context is, to me, a very pertinent point in the discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:53:59-07:00","id":529249,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean you, YeOfLittleFaith; sorry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The obvious quality of the writing of the second edition speaks for itself. I find the tone to be not to my taste; but that isn't criticism of the writers' work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:55:45-07:00","id":529250,"title":"","content":"Oh, alright then. And fair enough!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:10:14-07:00","id":529259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529201#post529201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. &quot;oh, no I could lose control and hurt someone I care about&quot; loses a lot of bite when <i>nobody fits that description. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's funny. There were <i><b>SO MANY </b></i>things that I care (cared?) about as a Werewolf in 1st Edition that I just cannot connect to whatever point you may be trying to make here. Assuming that there is a point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:22:12-07:00","id":529266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529259#post529259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's funny. There were <i><b>SO MANY </b></i>things that I care (cared?) about as a Werewolf in 1st Edition that I just cannot connect to whatever point you may be trying to make here. Assuming that there is a point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point being made was that the first edition (This is true of all of the first editions of nWoD, far as I can tell) doesn't really do much to mechanically support the notion that characters should have people to care about. Werewolf 2nd Edition allows you to create and control wolf-blooded and human members of the Pack, which, also including touchstones, actually does allow you to ground these characters you might care about in the mechanics of the game. It's about as necessary as any other game mechanic, in the sense that you don't <i>need </i>it to play make believe, but it does a nice job of adding some mechanical weight to your make believe, and hopefully that makes it a little bit more fun for people who may have felt iffy about it in the past.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't add to your experience, then you didn't want or need that mechanic, and that's great. For those who felt their games were lacking something, they now have mechanics to address that concern, and that's great too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:29:15-07:00","id":529273,"title":"","content":"That's a good point, Leetsepeak. First edition seemed to have the 'Apocalypse problem,' despite the unihar, in that it wasn't just possible but entirely likely you could have a game without encountering humans or wolf-blooded at all as anything beyond 'host to something' or 'background scenery.'<br /> <br /> With second edition, you're capable of bringing humans into your pack without letting them actually know it, not only giving you some incentive for looking out for them but others in your pack. More than capable, you're encouraged by the character and pack creation. There's a little Monsterhearts in there.<br /> <br /> And thankfully you aren't forced into playing spirit cops. It's certainly a theme you can play, as the examples show many of the targets of sacred hunts can be those who upset the territory, but you're no longer limited to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-26-2015, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:31:06-07:00","id":529276,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think the responses got muddled last page. Just to be clear, <i>I</i> was responding to BigDamnHero. That said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529199#post529199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the Forsaken are less Forsaken, in my opinion, if there are people in their pack - there is fewer reason for them to interact with ordinary people - less of a sense of isolation<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The humans in the pack <i>ARE</i> ordinary people. Some of them anyway. Those people you would be forced to interact with in first edition? Those are your packmates now. The only difference is that you can give them a bit of a boost from your totem and stuff. You have an insular little group, but now that group consists of 20 or so people instead of 6. Half of which are mortal or mostly mortal and can have nasty stuff happen to them. You haven't lost anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:41:21-07:00","id":529279,"title":"","content":"You're also still Forsaken by society. Like, I've felt like the comparison with gangs is really apt for the Pack, because the regular, mortal world does not adequately understand or engage with the needs or problems of the Werewolf community, so the Packs address that, offer a form of communal involvement and identity, and also serves to isolate the members from more conventional society. The pack mentality could almost seem like brainwashing with the kinds of ideas they put on pack members as Uratha.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying, I don't actually think the game is less Forsaken now than it was before, just because the Pack is slightly larger. Your 5-6 Uratha are now also parts of a group with more people that might also feel forsaken by society at large, and also by other werewolves in the form of the Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:16:24-07:00","id":529385,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that humans and other beings can be involved into the pack's business as &quot;honorary members&quot; and the 2nd edition seems full with so many thrilling new features as well. I think I'm going to buy it as soon as possible!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:38:47-07:00","id":529395,"title":"","content":"*Pokes head out of cartoon punch-up dust cloud* Awesome.Glad we could help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:56:06-07:00","id":529407,"title":"","content":"Can you explain me that &quot;tribal prey&quot; thing as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:22:17-07:00","id":529424,"title":"","content":"Each tribe has a prey they consider sacred, meaning its the one they think is the most dangerous threat, and thus the most worthy prey to hunt. They are not limited to hunting only that prey, but usually being part of tribe confers some easier-to-get benefits towards fighting that prey. Some tribal affinity gifts are more likely to be useful against their sacred prey than those of other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:44:44-07:00","id":529460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529407#post529407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain me that &quot;tribal prey&quot; thing as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>One common complaint about Tribes in 1e was that they were kind of just &quot;second auspices.&quot; Rahu were the Warrior Auspice, Blood Talons were the Warrior Tribe. Irraka were the Stalker Auspice, Hunters in Darkness were the Stalker Tribe. Irraka were the Spirit Guy Auspice, Bone Shadows were the Spirit Guy tribe, etc. To address this, 2e refined the concepts by making Auspice <i>how</i> you hunt, and Tribe <i>what</i> you hunt. That's not to say that a Bone Shadow can't hunt the Pure or a Blood Talon can't hunt spirits, but each Tribe considers a different kind of prey the most dangerous, and therefore the most worthy of the sacred hunt.<br /> <br /> Blood Talons claim other werewolves as their sacred prey (usually the Pure Tribes and Bale Hounds, but sometimes other Forsaken who have violated the Oath of the Moon in a big way). After all, what enemy could be more worthy to earn Glory in battle against than one that is your equal in every way?<br /> <br /> Bone Shadows claim spirits as their sacred prey. Unlike other prey, they cannot be destroyed by physical force alone, and even once defeated they are often not truly destroyed, making them the most worthy prey for the Wise hunter.<br /> <br /> Hunters in Darkness claim the Hosts as their sacred prey. These insidious vermin can slip into a hunter's territory unnoticed until the infestation has grown to nearly unmanageable size, destroy or seal shut the local gauntlet, and if even one shard escapes, the hive can live on to reform again elsewhere. There is no prey more worthy than that which even the Purest hunter could not defeat.<br /> <br /> Iron Masters claim humans as their sacred prey. While a lone human poses no serious threat to even the weakest of werewolves, human influence has an exceptionally powerful impact on both the physical world and the shadow. Any cub can slaughter a single human, but only a Cunning hunter can stand against the power structures that humans create, and that makes them the most worthy prey. Additionally, other creatrures often hide in human skin - vampires, mages, and stranger thing still. The Hunters in Darkness consider such prey to be within their purview as well.<br /> <br /> Storm Lords claim the Ridden as their sacred prey - humans who are Posessed, Urged, or Claimed by spirits. These twisted amalgams of spirit and flesh mock the nature of the Uratha and insult Father Wolf's memory. Any Honorable hunter should recognize why such abominations are the most worthy prey.<br /> <br /> The Idigam are the out-of-context problem. The Wolf Must Hunt, and the Moon-Banished and Earthbound are the only prey The Wolf Can't Hunt. They come from a time before the world was formed, when all was chaos, and embody concepts that no longer exist. They have no set Ban or Bane to exploit, making them near impossible to kill. If they coalesce - accept the laws of this constant, ordered universe, they take on a permanent Ban in the process, which puts them into a context the Uratha can deal with. But this process also makes them considerably more powerful, allowing them to turn their inner chaos out upon the worlds of spirit and flesh around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-26-2015, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T18:17:23-07:00","id":529470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529182#post529182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah? They've been a thing in first edition too.<br /> <br /> It's not gone. It's, in this poster's opinion, gone, largely, because the Forsaken in 2nd edition have it easier than the Forsaken in 1st edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it has it largely easier for all the things that prey on Uratha who would foolishly stick around their loved ones to induce them into killing frenzies that leave their very own packs no recourse but to murder them on the scene, or clean after a massacre, assuming the pack itself doesn't joins it. Specially when their bouts of Kuruth are largely unavoidable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T18:30:27-07:00","id":529477,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Ok guys, proponents of each edition have said their piece. Let's not let this thread devolve into edition warring, please.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T01:44:15-07:00","id":529684,"title":"","content":"Just a note, I am not attempting to argue which book is supposed to be better. I am merely expressing what changes have led me to favor 2nd ed over first ed. But here's my perspective on 1st and 2nd ed:<br /> <br /> Now I have yet to play 2nd ed, as I only got the book about 3 weeks ago and am still reading it. But I am really liking how much smoother the rules seem to be in 2nd ed. First ed I felt was too restricting with rules that dictated too much of what a werewolf could and could not do. I tried to run a 1st ed game with some of my gamer friends (who were Apocalypse players) and they felt the 1st ed system didn't allow them much freedom to tell their stories. The biggest complaints came from the confusing renown-gifts system (gifts had no consistency with their renown), the sin-based harmony feeling like a punishment for their actions, and the fact that the characters could only be in Gauru for a few rounds. <br /> <br /> Now, Gauru still is limited in duration in 2nd ed, but GOD IS IT POWERFUL! Plus you can push the limit risking Death Rage to stay in Gauru longer. The Harmony system is very interesting, and doesn't necessarily punish the players for doing what werewolves do until they go too far out of balance. I feel it's a lot more workable than the sin-based system. Also the Renown-Gift mechanics are much better in design then they were before. <br /> <br /> Now the great thing about second ed is that it allows for sandbox design and play, meaning that if there are elements from 1st ed that you want to incorporate into 2nd ed, you can go ahead and patch them in. Also, though the 2nd ed core may feel like it's lacking in some areas, I feel that those areas will get more coverage in future additions. This book is a good starter, and with a little ST elbow grease, it can be supplemented with other 1st ed werewolf books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:36:10-07:00","id":529935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529684#post529684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a note, I am not attempting to argue which book is supposed to be better. I am merely expressing what changes have led me to favor 2nd ed over first ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's totally reasonable and on-topic, so no need to worry. The whole point of the thread was to explain the differences between the editions and people's preferences. Just as long as we're keeping it constructive and not putting other people's preferences down, it's all good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T08:59:04-07:00","id":530011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=529684#post529684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a note, I am not attempting to argue which book is supposed to be better. I am merely expressing what changes have led me to favor 2nd ed over first ed. But here's my perspective on 1st and 2nd ed:<br /> <br /> Now I have yet to play 2nd ed, as I only got the book about 3 weeks ago and am still reading it. But I am really liking how much smoother the rules seem to be in 2nd ed. First ed I felt was too restricting with rules that dictated too much of what a werewolf could and could not do. I tried to run a 1st ed game with some of my gamer friends (who were Apocalypse players) and they felt the 1st ed system<i><b> didn't allow them much freedom to tell their stories</b></i>. The biggest complaints came from the confusing renown-gifts system (gifts had no consistency with their renown), the sin-based harmony feeling like a punishment for their actions, and the fact that the characters could only be in Gauru for a few rounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have me curious... What constraints on the character's individual stories did you experience in 1st Edition?<br /> I always considered the Renown-Gift Issues you see as a Feature, not a Bug, bit not everyone likes it, I know. Still, it is the bolded part above that has me curious, as I never experienced that particular issue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:07:37-07:00","id":530018,"title":"","content":"Personally I don't thing the 1st edition gift system was <i>bad</i> (individual gifts, not so much) but I took one look at second edition's and my immediate thought was &quot;holy shit, this is <i>so much better</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's like that for most of the changes, really. Off the top of my head I can't think of one I don't consider an improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:29:19-07:00","id":530049,"title":"","content":"What I don't like about gifts in 2nd edition is the fact that, other than moon gifts, they're all equally powerful. Unlike the first edition, the setting of 2nd edition doesn't easily allow for interesting things like ancient, vastly powerful gifts or simple tricks lacking in supernatural potency - it's all the same power level. I prefer the flexibility of 1st edition gifts, with gifts of variable power. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:32:55-07:00","id":530055,"title":"","content":"About half of them <i>do</i> scale though. It's just based off renown dots. And then there's Catastrophe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:48:07-07:00","id":530072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530049#post530049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't like about gifts in 2nd edition is the fact that, other than moon gifts, they're all equally powerful. Unlike the first edition, the setting of 2nd edition doesn't easily allow for interesting things like ancient, vastly powerful gifts or simple tricks lacking in supernatural potency - it's all the same power level. I prefer the flexibility of 1st edition gifts, with gifts of variable power.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why fetishes can modify how they work. For example: Oh look, Now I can have mind-chat with my packmates without having to see them. Oh look, now I can blanket an area that automatically causes people to gain Shadow Paranoia and/or Lured. Oh look, now I can shrug off supernatural attempts at gaining control of my mind with a display of force.<br /> <br /> And, if memory serves, some fetishes can be pretty damned legendary/powerful/ancient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T10:36:25-07:00","id":530113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530049#post530049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't like about gifts in 2nd edition is the fact that, other than moon gifts, they're all equally powerful. Unlike the first edition, the setting of 2nd edition doesn't easily allow for interesting things like ancient, vastly powerful gifts or simple tricks lacking in supernatural potency - it's all the same power level. I prefer the flexibility of 1st edition gifts, with gifts of variable power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's understandable. Personally, I find that to be a huge feature because I no longer have to go through the weak 1 and 2 dot Gifts (or pay extra xp to skip them) in order to get to the powers I actually want. But I can see how the loss of 4 and 5 dot powered Gifts could be an equally large drawback for some. For for me, the fact that most Facets scale with their associated Renown and the ability to improve on Facets with Fetishes is more than enough in the way of vertical advancement, and I'm glad that buying new Facets is more a matter of horizontal advancement. 1e Gifts always felt awkward to me because it seemed like they were trying to be both at the same time. Like, there was no way to get a low-key cold-based weather Gift or a an epic wind-based one, because Call the Breeze was one dot and Killing Frost was 4. Now, any Weather Facet I get starts out powerful enough to be appealing, but not overwhelming, and if I want to get better at one or the other, I just need to get more dots in the associated Renown.<br /> <br /> It's definitely a trade-off. It works for me because I tend to favor horizontal advancement in RPGs over vertical advancement, but if you really loved those five-dot Gifts, I can see how the new system might feel under-powered. Different strokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T11:04:02-07:00","id":530134,"title":"","content":"I would like to see more exploration of the &quot;Full Set Bonus&quot; thing some gifts had going. Like, Hunt Under Iron Skies is ok on it's own, but paired with the other weather gifts both it and they become a lot more useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T11:07:17-07:00","id":530136,"title":"","content":"It's also questionable whether the 4 or 5 dot gifts in first edition were that powerful, or would remain as such in second edition. The Technology gift has managed to incorporate the 2nd and 4th dot gifts of its first edition form into its second edition form, and is not the only one to do that, Mother Luna's first, second and fourth dot gifts having become wolf gifts. Full Moon's 4th dot gift allowed you an armor bonus, which could be simulated by wearing armor. Half-Moons 5th dot gift is ignored by the new Kuruth mechanics and the elodoth auspice gift is better anyways. And if you were playing a game that didn't have just werewolves and mortals, many of the first edition gifts simply had no effect, only working on those people.<br /> <br /> As for things you couldn't do in first edition, reproduce with another werewolf is one. You were taxed heavily if you wanted to be an efficient warrior, or bad guy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530134#post530134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see more exploration of the &quot;Full Set Bonus&quot; thing some gifts had going. Like, Hunt Under Iron Skies is ok on it's own, but paired with the other weather gifts both it and they become a lot more useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like that too. I believe Acrozatarim said that with Hunt of Fire and Ice, with the extreme cold version, you could turn Heavens Unleashed into a snowstorm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-27-2015, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T11:15:54-07:00","id":530139,"title":"","content":"The 5 dot crescent moon gift was just an extension of the 4 dot one. And had a massive xp tax if you wanted to get it on it's own. That shit had to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T11:50:14-07:00","id":530178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530136#post530136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also questionable whether the 4 or 5 dot gifts in first edition were that powerful, or would remain as such in second edition. The Technology gift has managed to incorporate the 2nd and 4th dot gifts of its first edition form into its second edition form, and is not the only one to do that, Mother Luna's first, second and fourth dot gifts having become wolf gifts. Full Moon's 4th dot gift allowed you an armor bonus, which could be simulated by wearing armor. Half-Moons 5th dot gift is ignored by the new Kuruth mechanics and the elodoth auspice gift is better anyways. And if you were playing a game that didn't have just werewolves and mortals, many of the first edition gifts simply had no effect, only working on those people.<br /> <br /> As for things you couldn't do in first edition, <b>reproduce with another werewolf is one</b>. You were taxed heavily if you wanted to be an efficient warrior, or bad guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded topic has been discussed quite a bit already. On the first page of this thread actually (possibly not the first page: I have 40 posts per page, which I understand is atypical). But best not to get back into it.<br /> <br /> At any rate, I don't think Christian A is talking about the <i>actual</i> power level of those Facets as much as the <i>idealized</i> power level, where you knew that elder werewolves were capable of unleashing the fury of the <i>hisil</i> made manifest upon you, often because they had been taught those powers by ancient and terrible spirit beings. When they could be arsed to get off of their lazy asses at any rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T12:53:48-07:00","id":530240,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean, those ancient werewolves have higher Renown and are probably slangin' Gifts you don't know if not ones you do know way, way better than you can, and that's not even getting into what their fetishes could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T13:33:36-07:00","id":530266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530011#post530011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have me curious... What constraints on the character's individual stories did you experience in 1st Edition?<br /> I always considered the Renown-Gift Issues you see as a Feature, not a Bug, bit not everyone likes it, I know. Still, it is the bolded part above that has me curious, as I never experienced that particular issue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I felt it forced me to make some awkward character building choices if I wanted to be effective. I could pick a Gift List I liked and take what ever Renown I needed to boost its dice pools, or pick a Renown and only take Gifts that used it in their dice pools, but if I built my character any other way I was left feeling weak, like I couldn't even get my own Gifts to work reliably. And with Renown being earned through deeds, it put serious constraints on how I would have to play my character in order to earn the appropriate Renown just to get my dice pools high enough to actually have my Gifts work consistently. Admittedly, this was in MeT's awful 8 div 3 card drawing system, so this issue may not have been as significant in the tabletop version of the rules, but that was my experience. In 2e, I feel much more free to just play my character the way I want to play them, and whatever Renown I end up earning naturally will unlock Facets that will be useful as soon as I get them, even at only 1 dot in the associated Renown, and automatically scale up if I earn more dots in that Renown. The whole system just feels far more intuitive and streamlined to me, instead of like a complex system of xp taxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T14:50:15-07:00","id":530334,"title":"","content":"Fair Enough - Thanks <i><b>Charlaquin</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T15:06:55-07:00","id":530344,"title":"","content":"I'll reiterate a response to Christian's issue with the &quot;flat&quot; power level of the Facets:<br /> <br /> It is incredibly easy to introduce more powerful Gifts. Just like 1e introduced Milestone Gifts, the same idea can be applied to 2e. Sufficiently powerful werewolves might gain access to either a new level of Gift with Facets that are much more potent than the base line ones, or it could work more like Wolf Gifts can you unlock Milestone Gift Facets are automatically unlocked when you earn whatever in-game requirements are put on it.<br /> <br /> The game doesn't currently support this (though VtR 2e doesn't currently support 6+ Disciplines either), but implementing them is not complicated if that's what you want and are willing to put in the work to design some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T18:06:21-07:00","id":530465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530266#post530266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt it forced me to make some awkward character building choices if I wanted to be effective. I could pick a Gift List I liked and take what ever Renown I needed to boost its dice pools, or pick a Renown and only take Gifts that used it in their dice pools, but if I built my character any other way I was left feeling weak, like I couldn't even get my own Gifts to work reliably. And with Renown being earned through deeds, it put serious constraints on how I would have to play my character in order to earn the appropriate Renown just to get my dice pools high enough to actually have my Gifts work consistently. Admittedly, this was in MeT's awful 8 div 3 card drawing system, so this issue may not have been as significant in the tabletop version of the rules, but that was my experience. In 2e, I feel much more free to just play my character the way I want to play them, and whatever Renown I end up earning naturally will unlock Facets that will be useful as soon as I get them, even at only 1 dot in the associated Renown, and automatically scale up if I earn more dots in that Renown. The whole system just feels far more intuitive and streamlined to me, instead of like a complex system of xp taxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you did the MET stuff, huh? You weren't in the Cam by any chance, were you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T19:43:32-07:00","id":530549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530049#post530049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't like about gifts in 2nd edition is the fact that, other than moon gifts, they're all equally powerful. Unlike the first edition, the setting of 2nd edition doesn't easily allow for interesting things like ancient, vastly powerful gifts or simple tricks lacking in supernatural potency - it's all the same power level. I prefer the flexibility of 1st edition gifts, with gifts of variable power.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the new gift structure, and believe they're mostly plenty powerful and flexible as written. I'm also glad that Werewolf decided to choose its own thematic direction, and not feel the need to mimic the long-standing power structure, even if may work in other games like Vampire or Mage. It definitely gives both Werewolf mechanics and culture a more unique feel.<br /> <br /> However, to the extent players want something that provides increasingly powerful mystic abilities for their characters, I believe the focus should be on fetishes. The lower level ones are useful, but the power levels increase dramatically with more dots, and fetishes can potentially do almost anything. They also reflect on a werewolves' unique relationship to spirits (at least until we see Mage 2e's Spirit Arcanum rules).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T19:51:03-07:00","id":530555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530465#post530465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, you did the MET stuff, huh? You weren't in the Cam by any chance, were you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was indeed. In Olympia, WA. I played a lot more with an independent troupe, but the Forsaken game I played in was Cam sanctioned... Sort of, anyway. Fun story, as we eventually learned, our ST was doing a LOT of stuff without seeking proper approval, and by the time he got caught it was waaaaaaaaay too late to ret-con his plots. So, they had Mt. St. Helens erupt to nuke the venue. The whole state was PISSED at him and he moved away shortly after (for unrelated reasons, but I imagine he was relieved to get away from all that negative attention.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T22:26:52-07:00","id":530699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530011#post530011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have me curious... What constraints on the character's individual stories did you experience in 1st Edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will elaborate. My player base was mostly composed of WtA Larpers. The old Laws of the Wild system allowed for a lot more freeform play, and that was what my friends were used to. But when I introduced them to NWoD 1st Ed, they were frustrated by all the restrictions. Part of it was my fault, because I mishandled some of the bookwork with modifiers and making my npcs flexible (I was a new ST at the time). But much of it too was the mechanics: the expensive XP costs; the sin-harmony mechanic, unihar, and kuruth feeling like a punishment for acting like a werewolf; the relative weakness of low dot gifts; and (as Charlequin put it) having to tailor your character towards specific renown in order to use specific gifts, and if your character didn't have that renown, gaining that renown was incredibly difficult. All of these factors put a lot of restrictions on the PCs, and they basically went from playing epic and badass werewolves to characters that were mostly just humans who could turn into rage monsters for a short time and were forced to hold back their powers lest they be punished in some way. That is what I meant by saying that the game mechanics didn't give them enough freedom to tell their stories. My players wanted to be epic, but they couldn't.<br /> <br /> I feel now that 2nd Ed has remedied much of the problems. The mechanics allow a character to be an epic werewolf: a badass hunter, even as a starting character, and the restrictions are much more reasonable to deal with. (Plus, I've grown as an ST, so I feel I won't make my own mistakes twice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T07:39:17-07:00","id":530999,"title":"","content":"Interesting... Thanks <i><b>Nuwisha Nutjob</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T15:27:12-07:00","id":531309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=530555#post530555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was indeed. In Olympia, WA. I played a lot more with an independent troupe, but the Forsaken game I played in was Cam sanctioned... Sort of, anyway. Fun story, as we eventually learned, our ST was doing a LOT of stuff without seeking proper approval, and by the time he got caught it was waaaaaaaaay too late to ret-con his plots. So, they had Mt. St. Helens erupt to nuke the venue. The whole state was PISSED at him and he moved away shortly after (for unrelated reasons, but I imagine he was relieved to get away from all that negative attention.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Given that I was the Global-level Forsaken ST for quite a while, it's surprising (or not, given how you phrased it) that I'm just now hearing about this. Weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T15:38:49-07:00","id":531322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=531309#post531309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Given that I was the Global-level Forsaken ST for quite a while, it's surprising (or not, given how you phrased it) that I'm just now hearing about this. Weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was all going on over my head, so I only heard the angry gossip surrounding the Mt. St. Helens eruption. I wouldn't be surprised if the rumor mill twisted the whole thing into something it wasn't. This was around two or three years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:02:16-07:00","id":531397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528989-what-s-new-in-2nd-edition?p=531322#post531322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was all going on over my head, so I only heard the angry gossip surrounding the Mt. St. Helens eruption. I wouldn't be surprised if the rumor mill twisted the whole thing into something it wasn't. This was around two or three years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that explains it, then. I left (for good) during the US/lots of affiliates split. Or whatever you want to call it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}